prd_rules[5]{pk,rule_name,section_pk,severity,summary}:
  1,identity_model_canonical_chain,1,critical,"Auth users, actors, and agent templates must remain distinct identity layers with explicit mappings."
  2,department_first_act_as_policy,3,critical,"Act-as eligibility is based on department intersection, not single-user ownership."
  3,actor_auth_user_lease_required,4,high,Auth-user-to-actor relationships must be represented in canonical lease/binding structures.
  4,visitor_identity_chain_primary,2,high,Visitor-facing routing must preserve actor attribution and deterministic fallback behavior.
  5,needs_review_must_define_review_reason,5,critical,Edges marked needs_review require explicit review_reason for agent queue routing.

